// process states 
//         shows where and how the process is working inside operating system / main memory and shows at what state of the execution is process is in . 

// process states : 
1) preemptive 
2) non premptive 

1) preemptive : forcefully stopped processs 
2) non preemptive : not forcefully stopped left to execute or run as much as wish 


1) process state diagram as preemptive :
new ------ ready ---- running -------terminated            // ready to running : interrupt 
              |            |                               // running to ready : schedular dispatch 
              waiting / blocked

// new to ready : the process all installed and resources are allocated eg : memory or some data given to process to start its execution 
// ready to running : the process is ready to run / execute or in ready state on cpu  to run 
// running : process is running or executing 
// termination : the process is terminated or exit / completed . 
// waiting / block : the process is waiting for the I/O operations . 
/// blocked to ready : all waiting process is ready to execute . 

// running --- termination : done by the processor itself .
// running ---  waiting / block : done by the processor itself .

// new to ready : done by the operating system .
// ready to running : done by the operating system .
// blocked to ready : done by the operating systenm .
// running to ready : (schedular dispatch ) done by the operating system .

// process states of non preemptive :
new ------ ready ---- running -------terminated         
              |            |                              // running to ready : schedular dispatch 
              waiting / blocked


// CPU vs I/O bound :
CPU : the processs is intensive in terms of the cpu operations .
I/O : If the process is intensive in terms of the I/O operations .

